WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.020
After the 1973 oil embargo,

2
00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:07.760
oil jumped from 2.90 to
11.65 dollars a barrel.

3
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:14.140
Over 1974, US consumer
prices rose 12.3 percent.

4
00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:15.680
And not just for oil.

5
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:19.540
Inflation is a rising price
level across the whole economy.

6
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:23.240
So what makes prices across a
whole economy keep going up?

7
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.960
In this mission, you'll
shift curves on an AD

8
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:30.260
and AS graph and track the
price level and real GDP.

9
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.310
Then you'll use a graph lab:

10
00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:36.220
move two sliders and watch how
the whole economy responds.

11
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.850
Your mission: figure out what
drives the price level up,

12
00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.480
and how to spot the cause.
